module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.LogRegularSaturationNormality
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Defs
import Sheaf.GroupTheory.SharpConeLatticeIntersection
import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Regular
import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Curve.Divisor
import Sheaf.RingTheory.SerreCriterionNormal
import WeilConjectures.RingTheory.SerreS2TotalFractionMembership
import Sheaf.RingTheory.CompleteToricBoundaryClassInjectivity
import Sheaf.RingTheory.CompleteToricFacetValuations

/-!
# Kato divisorial recognition on complete toric local models

Source: Illusie--Laszlo--Orgogozo, Exposé VI, 1.4 and 1.6(i)--(ii),
printed pp. 69--70 (blueprint: lem-trf-complete-toric-kato-recognition).

## Main definitions and statement

* `completeToricChart`: the canonical monomial map into the existing completed local model.
* `cohenCompleteToricRing`, `cohenCompleteToricChart`: its Cohen quotient and monomial map.
* `complete_toric_kato_recognition`: the recognition equality in both coefficient cases.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

open AlgebraicGeometry AddMonoidAlgebra

/-- The canonical chart sends `q` to the image of `z^q` in the completed model.
It is the composite of the monoid-algebra embedding, polynomial constants, and completion.
Source: ILO VI 1.6(i)--(ii), p. 70
(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-toric-kato-recognition). -/
noncomputable def completeToricChart (L : Type v) [CommRing L] [IsLocalRing L]
    (P : Type u) [AddCommMonoid P] (n : ℕ) : Multiplicative P →* CompletedLocalModel L P n :=
  (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin n) (AddMonoidAlgebra L P))
    (CompletedLocalModel L P n)).toMonoidHom.comp
      (MvPolynomial.C.toMonoidHom.comp (AddMonoidAlgebra.of L P))

/-- The complete Cohen quotient `B_C(P,n)/(θ)`, with its actual quotient-ring structure.
Source: ILO VI 1.6(ii), p. 70
(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-toric-kato-recognition). -/
abbrev cohenCompleteToricRing (C : Type v) [CommRing C] [IsLocalRing C]
    (P : Type u) [AddCommMonoid P] (n : ℕ) (θ : CompletedLocalModel C P n) :=
  CompletedLocalModel C P n ⧸ Ideal.span {θ}

/-- The canonical chart in the Cohen model is the completed chart followed by the quotient.
Source: ILO VI 1.6(ii), p. 70
(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-toric-kato-recognition). -/
noncomputable def cohenCompleteToricChart (C : Type v) [CommRing C] [IsLocalRing C]
    (P : Type u) [AddCommMonoid P] (n : ℕ) (θ : CompletedLocalModel C P n) :
    Multiplicative P →* cohenCompleteToricRing C P n θ :=
  (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {θ})).toMonoidHom.comp (completeToricChart C P n)

/-- In each of the two complete models, the preimage of localization units consists
exactly of a ring unit times a chart monomial. The two coefficient alternatives are
independent universally quantified clauses. No auxiliary coefficient ring is needed
in either clause. The fs predicate applies to the multiplicative tag of the same
additive monoid used by the monoid algebra.
Source: ILO VI 1.4 and VI 1.6(i)--(ii), pp. 69--70
(blueprint: lem-trf-complete-toric-kato-recognition).

Proof plan (the direct algebraic proof recorded in the node):
1. Apply `lem-trf-log-regular-saturation-normality` to get a nonzero normal domain.
   `lem-trf-complete-toric-facet-valuations` gives Noetherianity, nonzero monomials,
   facets, primitive forms, facet primes, and their monomial valuation formulas.
   `lem-trf-sharp-cone-lattice-intersection` gives a finite free group completion
   `G` and the equality `P = σ ∩ G`. These include the trivial monoid and `n = 0`.
2. Prime localizations are normal by clearing the finitely many denominators in
   an integral equation and rescaling its root. Their ideals are generated by
   images of generators of contracted ideals, hence they are Noetherian.
   `lem-sc-normal-dim1-dvr` identifies height-one localizations as DVRs; the
   normalized valuations of `def-sc-discrete-valuation-ring` test membership and units.
3. Apply `lem-sc-divisor-finite-support` to `Spec R`. DVR lengths identify its
   orders with these valuations. Principal divisors have finite support and add
   on products, so form their quotient class group as in the boundary-injection node.
4. If `f` is a localization unit, represent its inverse by `g/z^a`. Clear the
   localization equality by a monomial, then cancel that nonzero monomial in the
   domain to get `fg = z^a ≠ 0`. Outside the facet primes monomials are units by
   `lem-trf-complete-toric-facet-valuations`, so `f` is a unit there. Its divisor
   is therefore `∑ m_F [p_F]`, with all facet values `m_F` nonnegative.
5. This divisor has zero class. Apply
   `lem-trf-complete-toric-boundary-class-injectivity` with the data from step 1:
   its integer cokernel class is zero, so `m_F = ν_F(g₀)` for some `g₀ : G`.
6. The facet half-spaces put `g₀` in `σ`. Saturation via
   `lem-trf-sharp-cone-lattice-intersection` gives `g₀ = a₀` for `a₀ : P`.
7. The fraction `w = f/z^a₀` has valuation zero at every height-one prime by
   the facet valuation formula. Thus both `w` and its inverse lie in every
   height-one localization; at the only height-zero prime they already lie in the field.
8. Normality of prime localizations and `lem-weil-pbc-serre-criterion-normal`
   give S2. Apply `lem-weil-pbc-serre-s2-total-fraction-membership` to `w` and
   its inverse: both lie in `R`. Injection into its fraction field proves that
   `w` is a unit and `f = w z^a₀`.
9. Conversely a unit times a monomial becomes a unit in the localization.
   For trivial `P`, the facet vector is empty, `G = 0`, and the localization
   inverts only 1, so the equality reduces to the units of `R`. For `n = 0`
   all parameter-variable sets are empty.
-/
theorem complete_toric_kato_recognition
    (P : Type u) [AddCommMonoid P]
    (hP : IsFineSaturatedMonoid (Multiplicative P))
    (hsharp : ∀ q : P, IsAddUnit q → q = 0) (n : ℕ) :
    (∀ (k : Type v) [Field k],
      (algebraMap (CompletedLocalModel k P n)
        (Localization (Submonoid.map (completeToricChart k P n) ⊤))) ⁻¹' {x | IsUnit x} =
          {x | ∃ a : CompletedLocalModel k P n, IsUnit a ∧
            ∃ q : Multiplicative P, x = a * completeToricChart k P n q}) ∧
    (∀ (C : Type v) [CommRing C] [IsLocalRing C] (p : ℕ), IsCohenRing p C →
      ∀ θ : CompletedLocalModel C P n,
        θ - (p : CompletedLocalModel C P n) ∈ completedLocalModelBoundaryIdeal C P n →
        (algebraMap (cohenCompleteToricRing C P n θ)
          (Localization (Submonoid.map (cohenCompleteToricChart C P n θ) ⊤))) ⁻¹'
            {x | IsUnit x} =
          {x | ∃ a : cohenCompleteToricRing C P n θ, IsUnit a ∧
            ∃ q : Multiplicative P, x = a * cohenCompleteToricChart C P n θ q}) := by
  sorry
